        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:07 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Yellow Transportation, Inc. (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2002-01-270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b880b2e53d4260cdae9d27fb834f7b356e44d659bfaca3ab0d30f69d49527503",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b880b2e53d42-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The issue in this case is a narrow one, but it has considerable practical importance for the continuing flow of interstate commerce."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2002-01-270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b880b2e53d4260cdae9d27fb834f7b356e44d659bfaca3ab0d30f69d49527503",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b880b2e53d42-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: But did it waive the fee for all carriers in the State?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Yellow Transportation, Inc. (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2002-01-270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b880b2e53d4260cdae9d27fb834f7b356e44d659bfaca3ab0d30f69d49527503",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b880b2e53d42-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Base-plated means that plates, license plates, were issued by that State. So the State -- the title for the vehicles were in those States."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (Amicus Curiae)",
      "case_id": "2002-01-270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b880b2e53d4260cdae9d27fb834f7b356e44d659bfaca3ab0d30f69d49527503",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b880b2e53d42-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress assigned responsibility for implementing the single State registration system to the Interstate Commerce Commission. The ICC determined that when States apply the statutory fee cap, they must consider the reciprocal fee reductions and reciprocal fee waivers that were in place as of November 15th, 1991."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Schlick",
      "case_id": "2002-01-270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b880b2e53d4260cdae9d27fb834f7b356e44d659bfaca3ab0d30f69d49527503",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b880b2e53d42-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The ICC did, during the rulemaking proceeding, change its interpretation. As the D.C. Circuit said in NARUC v. ICC, that's what comment periods are for."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2002-01-270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b880b2e53d4260cdae9d27fb834f7b356e44d659bfaca3ab0d30f69d49527503",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b880b2e53d42-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The ICC's interpretation of the fee cap is a reasonable implementation of Congress's provision. It's consistent with the language of the statute and its purposes and we submit that it should be upheld. The decision of the Michigan Supreme Court should be reversed, and the case should be remanded."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2002-01-270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b880b2e53d4260cdae9d27fb834f7b356e44d659bfaca3ab0d30f69d49527503",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b880b2e53d42-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If it is not affirmed, however, we agree with the United States that the case should be remanded to the Michigan Supreme Court for consideration of this other issue which is still viable."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b880b2e53d4260cdae9d27fb834f7b356e44d659bfaca3ab0d30f69d49527503",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b880b2e53d42-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: In Michigan you -- you helpfully began your argument by pointing out that the case had been decided on a different ground below."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b880b2e53d4260cdae9d27fb834f7b356e44d659bfaca3ab0d30f69d49527503",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b880b2e53d42-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: I understand that. I'm -- I'm not worried about the sky falling, but I'm addressing your argument from the purpose of the statute. And you say the purpose is to preserve State revenues, but you come up with a theory that goes far beyond preserving State revenues. It permits the States to augment their -- their revenues considerably."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice",
      "case_id": "2002-01-270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b880b2e53d4260cdae9d27fb834f7b356e44d659bfaca3ab0d30f69d49527503",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b880b2e53d42-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: -- is that despite this Federal statute, you can terminate your reciprocity agreement with Kansas and charge the full $10. Right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "State of Michigan",
      "case_id": "2002-01-270",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b880b2e53d4260cdae9d27fb834f7b356e44d659bfaca3ab0d30f69d49527503",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b880b2e53d42-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Let me -- let me just close by saying that we believe that the Michigan Supreme Court's decision is faithful to the text, results in a consistent and a coherent interpretation of the Federal statute, that is consistent with the congressional intent, and we believe it should be affirmed."
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
